From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: run the RX IQ calibration gain sweep on radio 2057 rev 8

b43_nphy_rev3_cal_rx_iq() had the per-core setup and cleanup of the RX IQ
calibration and nothing in between. Behind that sit 7510 operations of an
MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057 rev
8), a third of an interface coming up. Fill in the three pieces that were
missing, which arrive together because none of them measures anything on
its own.

First, the frame around the per-core loop, which is the rest of
brcmsmac's wlc_phy_cal_rxiq_nphy_rev3(): clear the receive reset bit of
the baseband configuration and put the register back, hold the PHY in
carrier search for the whole calibration, save the transmit gain of the
two cores and program the gain the calibration asks for in its place,
skip a receive core that is switched off, reset the receive chain after
each core, and on the way out reset the carrier sense, drop the receive
gain override and put the saved gain back. Every piece of this is already
in b43: the gain comes from b43_nphy_iq_cal_gain_params(), which the
transmit IQ/LO calibration in this file uses for the same purpose, and
the state of the receive cores from b43_nphy_get_rx_core_state().

Second, b43_nphy_txpwr_index(), which is brcmsmac's
wlc_phy_txpwr_index_nphy() for a non-negative index: the sweep drives its
tone at a transmit power index its gain ladder names, and b43 had no way
to program one. b43_nphy_tx_power_fix() is a different job - it takes the
index from the SPROM, or hardcodes 30 on rev 7 and up, and does both
cores. The index selects one cell in each of four tables 128 cells apart
in the per-core power control table: the transmit gain at 192, the IQ
compensation at 320, the local oscillator compensation at 448, and on an
internal PA the RF power offset at 576. The capture shows all four reads
with the same index, so the layout is not taken on trust - the sweep uses
index 10, giving offsets 0xca, 0x14a, 0x1ca and 0x24a, and the tail of
the PAPD calibration uses index 30, giving 0xde, 0x15e, 0x1de and 0x25e.

Third, the sweep itself, brcmsmac's wlc_phy_rxcal_gainctrl_nphy_rev5() on
its rev 7 and up path: zero the receive IQ compensation, then walk a six
step ladder of receive gains - the two low pass filter biquad stages, the
second and first low noise amplifier - driving a tone at each step and
reading the power back from the IQ estimator. Above a threshold it steps
down, below it steps up, and it stops on the first step that crosses.
Then it trims the second biquad stage by the difference between the power
it wanted and the power it got, programs that, and puts the saved
compensation back.

Three things the reference has are deliberately not here. Its rxgain
output argument, because both of its call sites pass NULL and nothing
reads what it would return. Its 5 GHz ladder, because four of those six
steps ask for a fixed transmit gain rather than a power control index,
and that gain is built from a value b43 does not keep - the reference
reads it out of the transmit gain table, and the one line that would
store it in this file sits inside an #if 0. The caller is restricted to
2 GHz for that reason: a ladder step that cannot be programmed is worse
than a ladder that stops at the band the capture covers. And the negative
index of txpwr_index(), which replays state the reference saves on the
first call and that nothing in b43 asks for.

One difference from b43's own tx_power_fix is worth naming rather than
hiding: it narrows the DAC gain to three bits on rev 7 and up, where the
reference takes six. This takes six, because it is a port of the
reference. The capture cannot tell them apart - the field reads zero on
every call in it - so it is not decided by measurement.

Measured with test/phase_compare.py on the two contiguous-block windows:
up-ch1 goes from 5791 of 22951 to 11552 (25% to 50%), up-ch1-freddo from
8746 of 27571 to 13511 (32% to 49%), and PHY registers covered from 194
of 218 to 203. The shape matches too, and that is the stronger statement:
the capture has three iterations per core, each a transmit index followed
by a tone, and the port produces the same three per core, each as a run
of 85, 103, 85 and 420 matching operations.

One block of the previous measurement changes hands and it is not a
regression: the 172 operations at #13921, the two 84-cell clears of the
power control table, lose their assignment to one of the six identical
clears the sweep now performs, because the block assignment is exclusive
and greedy. Measured on that region alone the port is unchanged before
and after - the same 172 operations from the same position, 178 of 183.

What is still missing is the measurement the sweep sets the gain up for:
the tone at the requested calibration type and b43_nphy_calc_rx_iq_comp()
after it. So this still returns an error, deliberately - b43_phy_initn()
only calls b43_nphy_save_cal() when this returns zero, and there is no
calibration to save.

Verified: records #14951-#21136, from
"TBL.RD   id=0x0007 off=0x0110 len=2"
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n27304
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n28295
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n26855
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n241
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/23190a0/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/23190a0/test/phase_compare.py

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -3843,6 +3843,91 @@ static void b43_nphy_tx_power_ctrl(struct b43_wldev *dev, bool enable)
 		b43_nphy_stay_in_carrier_search(dev, 0);
 }
 
+/* Put one transmit chain on a chosen index of the power control table, the way
+ * brcmsmac's wlc_phy_txpwr_index_nphy() does for a non-negative index. The
+ * three tables the index selects sit 128 cells apart: the gain at 192, the IQ
+ * compensation at 320, the local oscillator compensation at 448, and on an
+ * internal PA the RF power offset at 576.
+ *
+ * Only the non-negative index is here. Handing the index back is a separate
+ * path in the reference, driven by state it keeps for the transmit
+ * calibrations, and nothing in b43 asks for it.
+ */
+static void b43_nphy_txpwr_index(struct b43_wldev *dev, u8 core_mask,
+				 u8 txpwrindex, bool restore_cals)
+{
+	struct b43_phy_n *nphy = dev->phy.n;
+	bool tx_pwr_ctrl_state;
+	u16 rad_gain, dac_gain, m1m2;
+	u16 iqcomp_a, iqcomp_b, regval[2];
+	u32 txgain, iqcomp, locomp;
+	s32 rfpwr_offset;
+	u8 bbmult, core, tbl;
+
+	if (nphy->hang_avoid)
+		b43_nphy_stay_in_carrier_search(dev, true);
+
+	for (core = 0; core < 2; core++) {
+		if (!(core_mask & (1 << core)))
+			continue;
+
+		tbl = core ? 27 : 26;
+
+		tx_pwr_ctrl_state = nphy->txpwrctrl;
+		b43_nphy_tx_power_ctrl(dev, false);
+
+		txgain = b43_ntab_read(dev, B43_NTAB32(tbl, 192 + txpwrindex));
+		rad_gain = (txgain >> 16) & 0x1FFFF;
+		dac_gain = (txgain >> 8) & 0x3F;
+		bbmult = txgain & 0xFF;
+
+		b43_phy_maskset(dev, core ? B43_NPHY_AFECTL_OVER :
+					    B43_NPHY_AFECTL_OVER1,
+				~0x0100, 0x0100);
+		b43_phy_write(dev, core ? B43_NPHY_AFECTL_DACGAIN2 :
+					  B43_NPHY_AFECTL_DACGAIN1, dac_gain);
+
+		b43_ntab_write(dev, B43_NTAB16(7, 0x110 + core), rad_gain);
+
+		m1m2 = b43_ntab_read(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 87));
+		if (core == 0)
+			m1m2 = (m1m2 & 0x00FF) | (bbmult << 8);
+		else
+			m1m2 = (m1m2 & 0xFF00) | bbmult;
+		b43_ntab_write(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 87), m1m2);
+
+		iqcomp = b43_ntab_read(dev, B43_NTAB32(tbl, 320 + txpwrindex));
+		iqcomp_a = (iqcomp >> 10) & 0x3FF;
+		iqcomp_b = iqcomp & 0x3FF;
+		if (restore_cals) {
+			regval[0] = iqcomp_a;
+			regval[1] = iqcomp_b;
+			b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 80 + 2 * core),
+					    2, regval);
+		}
+
+		locomp = b43_ntab_read(dev, B43_NTAB32(tbl, 448 + txpwrindex));
+		if (restore_cals)
+			b43_ntab_write(dev, B43_NTAB16(15, 85 + core), locomp);
+
+		if (b43_nphy_ipa(dev)) {
+			rfpwr_offset = b43_ntab_read(dev,
+					B43_NTAB32(tbl, 576 + txpwrindex));
+			b43_phy_maskset(dev, core ? B43_NPHY_PAPD_EN1 :
+						    B43_NPHY_PAPD_EN0,
+					~0x1FF0 & 0xFFFF,
+					(((s16)rfpwr_offset) << 4) & 0x1FF0);
+			b43_phy_set(dev, core ? B43_NPHY_PAPD_EN1 :
+					        B43_NPHY_PAPD_EN0, 0x4);
+		}
+
+		b43_nphy_tx_power_ctrl(dev, tx_pwr_ctrl_state);
+	}
+
+	if (nphy->hang_avoid)
+		b43_nphy_stay_in_carrier_search(dev, false);
+}
+
 /* https://bcm-v4.sipsolutions.net/802.11/PHY/N/TxPwrFix */
 static void b43_nphy_tx_power_fix(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 {
@@ -6003,16 +6088,217 @@ static void b43_nphy_rxcal_radio_cleanup(struct b43_wldev *dev, u8 core)
 	b43_radio_write(dev, atten, regs[1]);
 }
 
+/* One step of the receive gain ladder the RX IQ calibration walks: the two
+ * low pass filter biquad stages, the second and first low noise amplifier, and
+ * the transmit power index to drive the tone at. -1 there means drive it with a
+ * fixed gain instead of an index into the power control table.
+ */
+struct b43_nphy_rxcal_gain {
+	u16 hpvga;
+	u16 lpf_biq1;
+	u16 lpf_biq0;
+	u16 lna2;
+	u16 lna1;
+	s8 txpwrindex;
+};
+
+#define B43_NPHY_RXCAL_MAXGAININDEX	5
+#define B43_NPHY_RXCAL_TONEAMP		181
+#define B43_NPHY_RXCAL_TONEFREQ_20MHZ	2000
+#define B43_NPHY_RXCAL_TONEFREQ_40MHZ	4000
+
+enum b43_nphy_rxcal_dirn {
+	B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_INIT,
+	B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_UP,
+	B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_DOWN,
+};
+
+static const struct b43_nphy_rxcal_gain b43_nphy_rxcal_gaintbl_2ghz_rev7[] = {
+	{ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 10 },
+	{ 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 10 },
+	{ 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 10 },
+	{ 0, 0, 1, 3, 0, 10 },
+	{ 0, 0, 4, 3, 0, 10 },
+	{ 0, 0, 6, 3, 0, 10 },
+};
+
+/* Walk the gain ladder until the tone comes back at a workable power, then
+ * trim the second biquad stage so it lands on the power the calibration wants.
+ * brcmsmac's wlc_phy_rxcal_gainctrl_nphy_rev5(), the N-PHY rev 7 and up path.
+ *
+ * The rxgain output argument of the reference is not here: both its call sites
+ * pass NULL, so nothing ever reads what it would return.
+ *
+ * Neither is the 5 GHz ladder, and the caller keeps this to 2 GHz for it. The
+ * 5 GHz one asks for a fixed transmit gain rather than a power control index on
+ * four of its six steps, and that gain is built from a value b43 does not keep -
+ * the one the reference reads out of the transmit gain table, which this file
+ * computes inside an #if 0 and stores nowhere. A ladder step that cannot be
+ * programmed is worse than a ladder that stops at the band the capture covers.
+ */
+static void b43_nphy_rxcal_gainctrl(struct b43_wldev *dev, u8 rx_core,
+				    u8 cal_type)
+{
+	const struct b43_nphy_rxcal_gain *tbl = b43_nphy_rxcal_gaintbl_2ghz_rev7;
+	struct b43_phy_n_iq_comp save_comp, zero_comp = { };
+	struct nphy_iq_est est;
+	const u16 num_samps = 1024;
+	const u32 thresh_pwr = 10000;
+	const s16 desired_log2_pwr = 13;
+	u32 curr_pwr, optim_pwr = 0, prev_pwr = 0;
+	s16 actual_log2_pwr, delta_pwr;
+	u16 lpf_biq1, lpf_biq0, lna2, lna1;
+	u8 mix_tia_gain = 3;
+	s8 optim_idx = 0, prev_idx = 0, curr_idx = 3;
+	u8 dirn = B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_INIT;
+	bool done = false;
+	int fine_gain_idx;
+	u32 tone_freq;
+	/* Rev 7 and up transmit on the core being calibrated, earlier
+	 * revisions on the other one.
+	 */
+	u8 tx_core = rx_core;
+
+	b43_nphy_rx_iq_coeffs(dev, false, &save_comp);
+	b43_nphy_rx_iq_coeffs(dev, true, &zero_comp);
+
+	tone_freq = b43_is_40mhz(dev) ? B43_NPHY_RXCAL_TONEFREQ_40MHZ :
+					B43_NPHY_RXCAL_TONEFREQ_20MHZ;
+
+	do {
+		lpf_biq1 = tbl[curr_idx].lpf_biq1;
+		lpf_biq0 = tbl[curr_idx].lpf_biq0;
+		lna2 = tbl[curr_idx].lna2;
+		lna1 = tbl[curr_idx].lna1;
+
+		b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_one_to_many(dev,
+				N_RF_CTL_OVER_CMD_RX_GAIN,
+				(lpf_biq1 << 12) | (lpf_biq0 << 8) |
+				(mix_tia_gain << 4) | (lna2 << 2) | lna1,
+				0x3, false);
+
+		b43_nphy_txpwr_index(dev, 1 << tx_core,
+				     tbl[curr_idx].txpwrindex, false);
+
+		b43_nphy_tx_tone(dev, tone_freq, B43_NPHY_RXCAL_TONEAMP, false,
+				 cal_type, false);
+
+		b43_nphy_rx_iq_est(dev, &est, num_samps, 32, false);
+		if (rx_core == 0)
+			curr_pwr = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(est.i0_pwr, num_samps) +
+				   DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(est.q0_pwr, num_samps);
+		else
+			curr_pwr = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(est.i1_pwr, num_samps) +
+				   DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(est.q1_pwr, num_samps);
+
+		switch (dirn) {
+		case B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_INIT:
+			prev_idx = curr_idx;
+			if (curr_pwr > thresh_pwr) {
+				dirn = B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_DOWN;
+				curr_idx--;
+			} else {
+				dirn = B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_UP;
+				curr_idx++;
+			}
+			break;
+		case B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_UP:
+			if (curr_pwr > thresh_pwr) {
+				done = true;
+				optim_pwr = prev_pwr;
+				optim_idx = prev_idx;
+			} else {
+				prev_idx = curr_idx;
+				curr_idx++;
+			}
+			break;
+		case B43_NPHY_RXCAL_GAIN_DOWN:
+			if (curr_pwr > thresh_pwr) {
+				prev_idx = curr_idx;
+				curr_idx--;
+			} else {
+				done = true;
+				optim_pwr = curr_pwr;
+				optim_idx = curr_idx;
+			}
+			break;
+		}
+
+		/* Walked off either end of the ladder: keep the last index that
+		 * was on it.
+		 */
+		if (curr_idx < 0 || curr_idx > B43_NPHY_RXCAL_MAXGAININDEX) {
+			done = true;
+			optim_pwr = curr_pwr;
+			optim_idx = prev_idx;
+		} else {
+			prev_pwr = curr_pwr;
+		}
+
+		b43_nphy_stop_playback(dev);
+	} while (!done);
+
+	lpf_biq1 = tbl[optim_idx].lpf_biq1;
+	lpf_biq0 = tbl[optim_idx].lpf_biq0;
+	lna2 = tbl[optim_idx].lna2;
+	lna1 = tbl[optim_idx].lna1;
+
+	/* brcmsmac's wlc_phy_nbits() is the bit length of the absolute value,
+	 * which is what fls() returns and what this file already uses for the
+	 * same job in b43_nphy_calc_rx_iq_comp().
+	 */
+	actual_log2_pwr = fls(optim_pwr);
+	delta_pwr = desired_log2_pwr - actual_log2_pwr;
+
+	fine_gain_idx = (int)lpf_biq1 + delta_pwr;
+	if (fine_gain_idx + (int)lpf_biq0 > 10)
+		lpf_biq1 = 10 - lpf_biq0;
+	else
+		lpf_biq1 = max(fine_gain_idx, 0);
+
+	b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_one_to_many(dev, N_RF_CTL_OVER_CMD_RX_GAIN,
+			(lpf_biq1 << 12) | (lpf_biq0 << 8) |
+			(mix_tia_gain << 4) | (lna2 << 2) | lna1,
+			0x3, false);
+
+	b43_nphy_rx_iq_coeffs(dev, true, &save_comp);
+}
+
 static int b43_nphy_rev3_cal_rx_iq(struct b43_wldev *dev,
 			struct nphy_txgains target, u8 type, bool debug)
 {
 	struct b43_phy *phy = &dev->phy;
+	struct nphy_iqcal_params cal_params[2];
+	u16 gain_save[2], cal_gain[2];
+	u16 orig_bbcfg;
+	u8 rx_core_state;
 	u8 core;
 
-	/* Only radio 2057 rev 8 has been looked at against a capture. */
-	if (phy->rev != 8 || phy->radio_rev != 8)
+	/* Only radio 2057 rev 8 in 2 GHz has been looked at against a capture,
+	 * and the gain sweep only has the 2 GHz ladder.
+	 */
+	if (phy->rev != 8 || phy->radio_rev != 8 ||
+	    b43_current_band(dev->wl) != NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)
 		return -1;
 
+	orig_bbcfg = b43_phy_read(dev, B43_NPHY_BBCFG);
+	b43_phy_mask(dev, B43_NPHY_BBCFG, ~B43_NPHY_BBCFG_RSTRX & 0xFFFF);
+
+	b43_nphy_stay_in_carrier_search(dev, true);
+
+	/* The transmit gain of the two cores together, put back at the end, and
+	 * the gain the calibration wants in its place.
+	 */
+	b43_ntab_read_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(7, 0x110), 2, gain_save);
+	for (core = 0; core < 2; core++) {
+		b43_nphy_iq_cal_gain_params(dev, core, target,
+					    &cal_params[core]);
+		cal_gain[core] = cal_params[core].cal_gain;
+	}
+	b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(7, 0x110), 2, cal_gain);
+
+	rx_core_state = b43_nphy_get_rx_core_state(dev);
+
 	/* The frame the gain sweep runs inside, one core at a time: what
 	 * measures the tones and writes the IQ coefficients is not here yet, so
 	 * this hands the PHY over and takes it straight back. Returning an
@@ -6022,13 +6308,31 @@ static int b43_nphy_rev3_cal_rx_iq(struct b43_wldev *dev,
 	for (core = 0; core < 2; core++) {
 		b43_nphy_rxcal_phy_setup(dev, core);
 		b43_nphy_rxcal_radio_setup(dev, core);
-		/* The gain sweep goes here, brcmsmac's
-		 * wlc_phy_rxcal_gainctrl_nphy_rev5().
-		 */
+
+		if (rx_core_state & (1 << core)) {
+			b43_nphy_rxcal_gainctrl(dev, core, 0);
+			/* Measuring the tone and computing the coefficients
+			 * goes here: the tone at the calibration type this was
+			 * asked for, then b43_nphy_calc_rx_iq_comp().
+			 */
+		}
+
 		b43_nphy_rxcal_radio_cleanup(dev, core);
 		b43_nphy_rxcal_phy_cleanup(dev, core);
+		b43_nphy_force_rf_sequence(dev, B43_RFSEQ_RESET2RX);
 	}
 
+	b43_phy_write(dev, B43_NPHY_BBCFG, orig_bbcfg);
+
+	b43_nphy_reset_cca(dev);
+	b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_one_to_many(dev, N_RF_CTL_OVER_CMD_RX_GAIN, 0,
+					     0x3, true);
+	b43_nphy_force_rf_sequence(dev, B43_RFSEQ_RESET2RX);
+
+	b43_ntab_write_bulk(dev, B43_NTAB16(7, 0x110), 2, gain_save);
+
+	b43_nphy_stay_in_carrier_search(dev, false);
+
 	return -1;
 }
 
